      "body": "Adds one entry to **Tools, Workflows & Presets**.\n\n`dsh-triage` is the judgment layer for DSH plugins: it answers the two questions a profile owner\nactually has.\n\n**Before installing** — `dsh-triage check <pkg>` runs the same admission engine the launcher uses\nagainst your exact runtime, and `dsh-triage probe <pkg> --execute` installs a pinned candidate into\nan isolated `DSH_HOME` and records boot / http / render / inventory evidence (dry-run by default; the\nuser's profile is never touched). A `compat_verdict` agent tool exposes the same answer to the model,\nso an agent can ask before it installs anything.\n\n**After something breaks** — `dsh-triage why` names the mechanism instead of guessing: the row\nadmission denied, the module that failed to import, the capability that was declared but never\nregistered, the duplicate copy that shadowed a package. `dsh-triage audit` shows the current\ncomposition row by row, and a read-only settings tab renders the same numbers as the CLI.\n\nIt is deliberately narrow:\n\n- read-only (no install / remove / rollback — upstream `plugin_manager` owns that),\n- no credential access, no security claims (verdicts are `go` / `risky` / `blocked` / `unknown` with\n  per-claim evidence tiers, and `unknown` is a real answer),\n- MIT, DSH `>=0.2.0-rc.1 <0.3.0-0` (measured on 0.2.1-rc.4).\n\nThe repo also publishes a format-1 market index of versions it has actually measured `go`:\n`https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jjjjjjjjnnjnn/dsh-triage/main/docs/market/index.json`\n\n- Repo: https://github.com/jjjjjjjjnnjnn/dsh-triage\n- Licence: MIT\n- Star count is 0 at submission time; every other row carries a live count, so the line is formatted\n  the same way and can be updated as it grows.\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nEnhancements:\n- Add dsh-triage to the English and Chinese Tools, Workflows & Presets listings as a read-only plugin diagnosis and attribution tool.",
